Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-17-2001||01:38 PM||||I want to install a caddy 4.9, and keep my isuzu 5spd.. Will it take it and mount up? ALso, the caddy computers were set to auto's, how would I go about making it a stick shift? would i HAVE to change it to carburation, or is there another way?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||04-17-2001||02:17 PM||||The engine bolts right up. You'll need a custom flywheel with 8 holes and neutral ballance. I am working with Terryk (well actually he's doing all the work) on developing a chip to run the PFI in a Fiero with a 5 speed. Superchips can also burn a chip for it.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||04-17-2001||05:25 PM||||e-mail joe, he can answer and question about these engines<BR>bublucy@sympatico.ca <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx</A> <P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||04-17-2001||05:52 PM||||Johnny:<BR>Gotta love your persistence.  Months of bitchin' about clutches and you want to keep a stick.....<BR>crunch..crunch||||reg||6
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||04-17-2001||07:01 PM||||For some reason, which is probably obvious to a mechanic that has a lot more knowledge of how clutches work than me, when you use the Fiero tranny with an adapter plate ,good clutch and flywheel attached to a V8, the classic Fiero clutch problems seem to diasappear.  My Fiero when it was stock gave me as much grief as anyone elses here on the forum has had.  I'd have to push the pedal practically thru the floor for it to disengage.  Now it disengages halfway down and smooth as silk.  Go figure.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bubbajoexx||04-17-2001||07:06 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR> You'll need a custom flywheel with 8 holes and neutral ballance. * holes or do my eyes decieve me there are only 6 <P>||||reg||12
Z||000006||Archie||04-17-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Richard Parnell:<BR><B>For some reason......when you use the Fiero tranny with an adapter plate ,good clutch and flywheel attached to a V8, the classic Fiero clutch problems seem to diasappear. ...... Now it disengages halfway down and smooth as silk.  Go figure.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Very good point...... upon reading your message, I realized that the only time I actually think about " the classic Fiero clutch problems" is when someone calls or EMails me asking for help solving clutch problems with their stock Fiero. I get 2 or 3 of those EMails/calls a day.<P>Archie||||reg||1
